 "name": "ST09MILITARY.BBQ",
 "strings": [
  "",
  "There was an admiral named Tianem.",
  "Of the Earth Federation Forces.",
  "Admiral.",
  "Given that title,",
  "he likely had a navy background.",
  "Revil, so often compared with him,",
  "was a general, an army title,",
  "so it seems",
  "the Earth Federation space forces",
  "still dragged along the history",
  "and air of the ground era.",
  "He was a great commander.",
  "In later times, a warship",
  "bearing his name would appear.",
  "His record is full of lost battles.",
  "Utterly forsaken",
  "by the fortunes of war,",
  "such was this great commander.",
  "In strategy and tactics he was",
  "no worse than the senior officers",
  "of Zeon, run so much like",
  "a family business; in fact,",
  "he was the better man.",
  "But below strategy and tactics,",
  "in combat itself, he went on",
  "fighting through the early war",
  "with an almost unbroken losing run.",
  "He was",
  "a soldier fated",
  "to lose to new weapons.",
  "Thrashed by the Musai and Zaku,",
  "he then died to the Big Zam.",
  "Why such a man, frankly",
  "rather lackluster, is hailed",
  "as a great commander",
  "comes down to one reason.",
  "He fought bravely in one battle,",
  "and for that, his name shines on",
  "in Universal Century history.",
  "Operation British",
  "Pride of an Old Soldier",
  "Operation British was",
  "the code name Zeon gave it.",
  "A plausible reason for the name",
  "is on record,",
  "but it is surely a later stretch.",
  "At the time, the operation",
  "had to stay as secret as possible,",
  "so the Zeon military,",
  "wary of enemy intelligence,",
  "presumably gave it a name",
  "with no meaning.",
  "Later generations called",
  "this operation simply",
  "\"the colony drop.\"",
  "It was in the battle",
  "fought to stop this colony drop",
  "that Tianem made his name.",
  "Tianem was an old-school soldier.",
  "He was left behind by the times,",
  "toyed with by new weapons,",
  "and then he died.",
  "Yet of such a man, no, precisely",
  "for being such a man, history",
  "at times demands great deeds.",
  "Whether he wanted that,",
  "no one knows.",
  "He was probably",
  "a fierce commander, but",
  "never the stuff of a great one.",
  "But he",
  "had to become a great commander.",
  "Such was the fate of the man.",
  "Quite literally to protect Earth,",
  "he would fight bravely, throwing",
  "away his men's lives and his own.",
  "Zeon, political offspring of space",
  "dwellers crying for independence,",
  "turned to ruthless means",
  "to overturn",
  "the 50:1 gap in national power.",
  "A giant artificial body 30 km long",
  "floating in the heavens,",
  "the very home they lived in,",
  "a space colony:",
  "this they tried to drop on Earth.",
  "The author of the plan,",
  "it is said, was a man who had long",
  "studied colony drops since before",
  "the war, a man of extreme",
  "political creed:",
  "Colonel Aiguille Delaz.",
  "He branded the people",
  "of the colony \"Island Iffish\"",
  "as traitors who had defied Zeon",
  "and sided with the Federation,",
  "purged them with poison gas,",
  "fitted nuclear pulse engines,",
  "and set it on a course for Earth.",
  "Even a 50 m meteorite",
  "is deadlier than a tactical nuke:",
  "such is a mass weapon.",
  "Hollow inside though it was,",
  "a space colony, far larger still,",
  "would wreak devastation",
  "on a scale",
  "no one could imagine.",
  "Tianem's Earth Federation fleet",
  "with great valor.",
  "Quite literally, this was",
  "a battle to defend the Earth,",
  "and a mission dwarfing anything",
  "Amuro would later face",
  "fell to one outdated admiral",
  "and the sailors under him",
  "to carry on their own.",
  "The Federation's last-ditch stand",
  "bore no fruit in the end.",
  "But half their wish came true.",
  "Island Iffish,",
  "after entering the atmosphere,",
  "broke apart into three.",
  "Of the shattered",
  "Island Iffish,",
  "the heaviest piece,",
  "the spaceport section, struck",
  "Sydney, Australia, head-on,",
  "gouging out a giant crater",
  "now known as Sydney Bay",
  "and wiping out the populace.",
  "Nearly a fifth of Australia",
  "vanished, and the countless",
  "fragments from the breakup",
  "rained down across the globe.",
  "Cold snaps and tsunamis followed",
  "for days, inflicting on the Earth",
  "for years to come",
  "enormous lasting harm.",
  "The Earth's rotation,",
  "through this folly of mankind,",
  "would be sped up",
  "by 1.2 seconds per hour."
 ]
}
